## 🔹 What are Meta Tags?

Meta tags provide information about an HTML webpage to browsers, search engines, and other web technologies.

Meta tags are placed inside the `<head>` section of an HTML document.

Example:

```html
<meta name="description" content="My HTML learning journey">
```

Meta tags generally do not appear directly as visible content on the webpage.

---

## 🔹 Important Meta Tags

### 1. Character Encoding

```html
<meta charset="UTF-8">
```

UTF-8 allows webpages to correctly represent a wide range of characters and languages.

### 2. Viewport

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
```

This helps webpages display correctly on different screen sizes and is important for responsive web development.

### 3. Description

```html
<meta name="description" content="My HTML learning journey">
```

Provides a description of the webpage.

### 4. Keywords

```html
<meta name="keywords" content="HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Web Development">
```

Specifies keywords related to the webpage.

### 5. Author

```html
<meta name="author" content="Manoj">
```

Specifies the author of the webpage.

### 6. Refresh

```html
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="10">
```

Can be used to refresh the page after a specified number of seconds.

